1
00:06:37,894 --> 00:06:43,894
Déjà vu is thought to be a trick of the mind... but what if it's not?

2
00:13:15,789 --> 00:13:21,789
Déjà Vu is a action, thriller, science fiction film directed by Tony Scott.

3
00:19:53,684 --> 00:19:59,684
Called in to recover evidence in the aftermath of a horrific explosion on a New Orleans ferry, Federal agent Doug Carlin gets pulled away
from the scene and taken to a top-secret government lab that uses a time-shifting surveillance device to help prevent crime.

4
00:26:31,578 --> 00:26:37,578
Doug Carlin, played by Denzel Washington.

5
00:33:09,473 --> 00:33:15,473
Claire Kuchever, played by Paula Patton.

6
00:39:47,368 --> 00:39:53,368
Paul Pryzwarra, played by Val Kilmer.

7
00:46:25,263 --> 00:46:31,263
Carroll Oerstadt, played by Jim Caviezel.

8
00:53:03,157 --> 00:53:09,157
Denny, played by Adam Goldberg.

9
00:59:41,052 --> 00:59:47,052
Gunnars, played by Elden Henson.

10
01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
Déjà Vu is a 2006 American science fiction action thriller film directed by Tony Scott,
written by Bill Marsilii and Terry Rossio, and produced by Jerry Bruckheimer.

11
01:12:56,842 --> 01:13:02,842
The film stars Denzel Washington, Paula Patton, Jim Caviezel,
Val Kilmer, Adam Goldberg and Bruce Greenwood.

12
01:19:34,736 --> 01:19:40,736
It involves an ATF agent who travels back in time in an attempt to prevent a domestic terrorist
attack that takes place in New Orleans and to save a woman with whom he falls in love.

13
01:26:12,631 --> 01:26:18,631
Filming took place in New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina.

14
01:32:50,526 --> 01:32:56,526
The film premiered in New York City on November 20, 2006, and was
released in the United States and Canada on November 22, 2006.

15
01:39:28,421 --> 01:39:34,421
It received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $180.6 million
worldwide against its $75 million production budget.

16
01:46:06,315 --> 01:46:12,315
It was the 23rd most successful film worldwide for 2006.

17
01:52:44,210 --> 01:52:50,210
The film explores themes of deja vu, technology, fbi,
patriotism, new orleans, louisiana.

18
01:59:22,105 --> 01:59:28,105
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
